00:00:05.641 --> 00:00:08.210
Zoe: Circumstances in which it
can sometimes be important to

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:12.710
disclose confidential information
is when there's a safety issue.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:16.340
So when sharing information is in
the best interest of the safety

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:17.600
of the child or young person.

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:21.270
Even then, it's important to explain
to the child, or young person that

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:22.730
you plan to share that information.

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:27.630
Ellen: When it comes to
safeguarding concerns, we have

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.550
to protect that young person.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:36.600
Say if they came to us with really
serious information, like they might say

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:39.240
"such and such has happened at home".

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:44.190
You know, they might say to us, "oh
please, can you not tell anyone?"

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:47.880
But we can't promise that we have
to say, "look, we don't want to,

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:52.710
but, to protect you we might have
to tell our safeguarding lead".

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:57.660
Phil: It was discovered that there was
a safeguarding issue then obviously

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:02.420
that would need to be shared with the
designated safeguarding lead and the

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:06.980
appropriate step following a safeguarding
policy, basically, but that's if there

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:14.040
was a need and which is why, again, you
can't promise a young person that you'll

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:19.380
keep something confidential because there
may be a safeguarding issue, somebody

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:23.369
may be at risk themselves or others,
and that information would need to be

00:01:23.369 --> 00:01:25.140
passed up for safeguarding reasons.

00:01:25.479 --> 00:01:29.090
Zoe T: Really it's just, if it's a
safeguard in issue, if it's going to

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:32.949
cause harm to that person or they're
going to cause harm to somebody else.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.539
I mean, there isn't really
any justification for

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:40.340
breaching confidentiality
under any other circumstances.

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:44.870
Phil: Information to be shared with
other staff only if there was a

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:48.090
risk  and it needed to be shared.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:52.050
And again, that would probably
be staff higher up that that

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:55.390
need to know not all staff would
need to be aware of every detail.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:59.540
Kerry: And then it's things
like on a need to know basis.

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:03.320
It shouldn't just be, for example,
chatted about in the staff room.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:08.390
Say medication as an example, not
everybody that works here needs

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:12.440
to know what medication child A
is on, but the people who work

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:19.820
with him and those that give that
medication halfway through the day.

